.claude/worktrees/

# WS-K-6 — update signing key material. The PUBLIC key lives in
# tauri.conf.json (safe, meant to be distributed with the app); the PRIVATE
# key and its password are the Owner's alone, stored in a password manager,
# and must never exist inside this repository at all. These patterns are a
# safety net against an accidental `tauri signer generate` run without an
# explicit `-w` path pointing elsewhere.
*.key
*.key.pub
*.minisign
stockiha-update-signing*

# WS-K-7 — licence signing key material. Same posture as WS-K-6 above: only
# the PUBLIC keys are meant to be distributed with the app and are explicitly
# un-ignored below. The licence-signing PRIVATE key and its password are the
# Owner's alone (see scripts/licence/README.md) and must never exist inside
# this repository. `test-fixtures/` holds a deliberately public, test-only
# key pair (see src-tauri/licence/test-fixtures/) that is safe to commit and
# is explicitly un-ignored as well.
!src-tauri/licence/licence-public.key
!src-tauri/licence/test-licence-public.key
!src-tauri/licence/test-fixtures/
!src-tauri/licence/test-fixtures/*.key
scripts/licence/out/
